# What Prettier must not touch (ENT-214).
#
# Read this before adding a path. Most entries are here because reformatting
# the file would actively break something, not because the diff would be
# large, and the two cases are worth telling apart.

# --- Files another tool owns ---------------------------------------------
#
# gen/ is generated by `buf generate`, committed, and CI fails on any drift
# between the committed bytes and a fresh run. Formatting it would put this
# repository permanently one `buf generate` away from red.
gen/

# postman/ is edited by hand, and AGENTS.md says in as many words not to
# reformat it: loading and re-dumping the collection expands the compact
# arrays and escapes the section signs, turning a six-line change into a
# two-hundred-line diff nobody can review. Prettier would do exactly that in
# one pass.
postman/

# Written by tooling that will rewrite them in its own style the next time it
# runs, so formatting them buys a check that fails on somebody else's edit.
.claude/
.mcp.json
skills-lock.json
bun.lock

# --- Content, not code ----------------------------------------------------
#
# The regulation corpus: GDPR, the AI Act, EDPB guidelines and enforcement
# decisions. Source data whose shape is meaningful to the people who maintain
# it and whose diffs should show changed law, not changed whitespace.
data/corpus/

# The logo, hand-authored as HTML and SVG. A drawing rather than a document:
# its indentation tracks the shape of the mark, and normalising it makes the
# next edit to the artwork harder rather than easier.
docs/brand/

# Vendored from the AI Elements shadcn registry and owned upstream, patched
# only where types collide with @base-ui/react. eslint.config.mjs ignores it
# for the same reason: formatting it turns every upstream update into a
# conflict.
apps/web/components/ai-elements/

# --- Out of scope ---------------------------------------------------------
#
# ENT-214 formats the TypeScript workspace. Markdown and YAML are excluded
# deliberately rather than by oversight: the prose in this repository is
# hand-wrapped to carry emphasis, and the workflow and compose files carry
# long comments in the same style. Prettier would renormalise both to no
# benefit anyone can see. Widen this later if it earns its keep, in its own
# commit.
*.md
*.yml
*.yaml

# --- Build output ---------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.next/
out/
build/
coverage/
apps/web/test-results/
apps/web/playwright-report/
apps/web/blob-report/
next-env.d.ts

# The Python workspace's virtualenv (ENT-218). uv rebuilds it from uv.lock in
# seconds, and Prettier would otherwise walk several thousand vendored JSON
# files inside it. The failure is developer-only and therefore the confusing
# way round: CI never runs `uv sync` in the job that checks formatting, so a
# green pipeline sits alongside a red `format:check` on the machine of anyone
# who has run the tests.
apps/intelligence/.venv/

# Model weights (ENT-235). Gigabytes of binary that Prettier tries to read as
# a string and then fails on, with "Invalid string length", before reporting
# that everything it could read was fine. The directory is tracked (for its
# .gitignore) and its contents are not, so without this entry a developer who
# has run the stack has a `format:check` that errors on their own machine and
# not in CI, which is the confusing way round.
deploy/models/
